# Validation Standardization

## Core Requirements
- Shared validators for common cases
- No regex duplication
- Consistent error messages
- Type-safe validation

## Common Validators
```typescript
// Required fields
const required = (value: any) => !!value || 'This field is required'

// Email format
const email = (value: string) => {
  const pattern = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/
  return pattern.test(value) || 'Invalid email format'
}

// Phone numbers (as strings)
const phone = (value: string) => {
  const pattern = /^\+?[\d\s-]{10,}$/
  return pattern.test(value) || 'Invalid phone number'
}
```

## Implementation Guidelines
1. Use Zod for schema validation
2. Centralize validation logic
3. Reuse validation patterns
4. Implement proper error handling

## Validation Locations
- Form Validation: [src/components/ui](mdc:src/components/ui)
- API Validation: [src/services](mdc:src/services)
- Data Validation: [src/lib](mdc:src/lib)

## Best Practices
- Validate data at boundaries
- Use type-safe validation
- Provide clear error messages
- Handle edge cases properly

